    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895-a2">

                <pb facs="1030" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg836"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Appendix B—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Message to the London Munitions
                        Assignments Board</hi></p>
                <p>Until the countries which are members of the European Advisory Commission have
                    agreed upon a disposal policy, and until such an agreed policy is implemented,
                    the London Munitions Assignments Board is authorized to assign surrendered or
                    captured enemy materiel (<hi rendition="#underline">unless it is of non-German
                        origin</hi>)<anchor n="†" xml:id="d895-f1"/> in the hands of British- or <pb
                        facs="1031" n="837" xml:id="pg837"/> American-commanded forces in Austria
                    and Germany to the forces of those countries which will use such materiel in
                    furtherance of the agreed strategy in the war
                    against Japan.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
